00:05:16,666 --> 00:05:22,666
You call. They'll answer.

2
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:39,333
Talk to Me is a horror film directed by Michael Philippou.

3
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:56,000
When a group of friends discover how to conjure spirits using an embalmed hand, they become hooked on the
new thrill, until one of them goes too far and unleashes terrifying supernatural forces.

4
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:12,666
Mia, played by Sophie Wilde.

5
00:26:23,333 --> 00:26:29,333
Jade, played by Alexandra Jensen.

6
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Riley, played by Joe Bird.

7
00:36:56,666 --> 00:37:02,666
Daniel, played by Otis Dhanji.

8
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:19,333
Sue, played by Miranda Otto.

9
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Hayley, played by Zoe Terakes.

10
00:52:46,666 --> 00:52:52,666
Talk to Me is a 2022 Australian supernatural horror film directed by Danny and Michael Philippou in their feature
directorial debuts and written by Danny Philippou and Bill Hinzman, based on a concept by Daley Pearson.

11
00:58:03,333 --> 00:58:09,333
It stars Sophie Wilde, Alexandra Jensen, Joe Bird, Otis Dhanji, Miranda Otto, Zoe
Terakes, Chris Alosio, Marcus Johnson, and Alexandria Steffensen.

12
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
The film follows a group of teenagers discovering they can contact
spirits using a mysterious severed and embalmed hand.

13
01:08:36,666 --> 01:08:42,666
Talk to Me premiered at the Adelaide Film Festival on 30 October 2022, and was released by Maslow Entertainment, Umbrella
Entertainment, and Ahi Films in Australia on 27 July 2023 and by A24 in the United States the following day.

14
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed $92 million worldwide against a
production budget of $4.5 million, becoming A24's highest-grossing horror film.

15
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:16,000
At the 13th AACTA Awards, it won eight awards including the Best Film, the Philippou brothers won
for Best Direction and Best Original Screenplay, and Wilde won for Best Actress.

16
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
The film explores themes of suicide, trauma,
possession, female friendship, addiction.

17
01:29:43,333 --> 01:29:49,333
The tone is dark.
